+# Advisory file lock for `core-storage` cross-process coordination (iOS
+# main-app ↔ NSE / Android multi-process). Mirrors R100
+# `MXDatabase.swift:1116-1206 acquireFileLock(exclusive:)` — Phase 2
+# `schema.md §1.3` constrains NSE to a single-table push.db but KEK
+# rotation / migration apply still race across processes. `fs2 0.4`
+# wraps BSD `flock(2)` / Win32 `LockFileEx` behind one trait; pinned to
+# the last 0.4 release because 0.5 has not shipped and the API surface
+# we use (`FileExt::{lock_exclusive,try_lock_exclusive,unlock}`) has
+# been stable since 0.2.
+fs2 = "0.4"
+
 # Compile-time guarantee that key material is zeroed on drop.
 # Justification: schema.md §1.6 states `device_seed` / `KEK_user` / `DEK_user`
 # / `ws_dek` are all 32-byte secrets. `Zeroizing<[u8; 32]>` ensures these
