-**Goal:** Build `bindings/electron/` — a napi-rs native module that exposes mxcore's IKey crypto, push-frame decoding, AppContext + ServerClock, and PushTransport long-lived connection to Node.js / Electron applications, with idiomatic JS class API and Win x64 + macOS arm64 platform coverage.
-
-**Architecture:** Standalone cargo project at `bindings/electron/Cargo.toml` (NOT in workspace `members`). Depends on `core-ffi`, `core-context`, `core-transport`, `core-crypto`, `core-protocol` as path deps; consumes their **Rust API directly** (not C ABI). napi-rs `#[napi]` macros expose JS classes with auto-generated `.d.ts`. `tokio_rt` feature shares one tokio runtime between napi-rs and mxcore. `ThreadsafeFunction` bridges JS callbacks (rng / register-info) and event fan-out across the tokio-worker / V8 boundary.
-
-**Tech Stack:** Rust 1.83 + napi-rs 2.x + napi-derive + napi-build + @napi-rs/cli + vitest + Node 18+ / Electron 19+ (napi6 ABI).
