-## Spec Deviations (from `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-04-mxcore-electron-napi-binding-design.md`)
-
-The spec was written against `mxcore.h` (C ABI). When implementing against the Rust API, several field names and constructor shapes differ. The plan follows the Rust API verbatim — these deviations should land in the spec as a follow-up edit, not block implementation:
-
-| Spec said | Reality (Rust API) |
-|---|---|
-| `new IKey(secretKey: Buffer)` | `IKey::new(ikey: &[u8], uid: &str)` — uid is required (HKDF salt) |
-| `AppContextInit { appId, appVersion, appBuild, appBundle, deviceId, ... }` (13 flat fields) | Builder: `AppInfo::new(client_type, version, pkg, build)` (4) + `DeviceInfo::new(device_id, os_ver, client_name, client_number, model)` (5) + `LocaleSettings::new(language, language_list, region)` (3). Plan exposes a single flat `AppContextInit` to JS but maps internally |
-| `AppContext.login(userId, workspaceId)` | `ctx.user_session().login(UserSession::new(uid, space_id, rid))` — needs `rid` (resource id) too |
-| `PushRegInfo { apiKey, apiKeyId, padding, timestampMs, voipToken, pushToken }` | Real `PushRegInfo` has none of those — they live on `RegisterContext` (`ikey`, `rng_fn`, `time_fn`, `device_type_byte`). Real fields: `uid / space_id / rid / loc / network / device_key / model / os / client_version / os_version / is_appex / tenant_id` (12) |
-| `TransportEvent` 9 kinds | Actual: ~22 kinds (incl. `FrameReceived`, `HeartbeatSent`, `AckReceived`, `WireTx/Rx`, `PushRegEncoded/Wire/ZipMeta`, `DialStarted`, `NetworkAvailabilityChanged`). Plan exposes ALL kinds |
-
-The plan's tests verify the Rust API — not the spec field names — so spec drift is recorded but doesn't block.
