-//! `PushTransport` JS class — wraps `core_transport::PushTransport`.
-//!
-//! Lifecycle:
-//! 1. `PushTransport.create(opts)` → spawns supervisor + event-loop task.
-//! 2. The event-loop task `await`s `transport.next_event()` in a loop.
-//!    Each event is run through `transport_events::event_to_js` and
-//!    fanned out to all `ThreadsafeFunction`s registered for that
-//!    event name via `on()`.
-//! 3. `shutdown()` sends `Outbound::Shutdown`, waits for the supervisor
-//!    join (≤500ms), then aborts.
-//! 4. `Drop` cancels the event-loop task and aborts the supervisor.
