-## 1. Goal
-
-Provide a Node.js / Electron-loadable binding for mxcore so a Windows-first Electron client (with macOS dev parity) can call IKey crypto, push-frame decoding, AppContext metadata + ServerClock, and the full PushTransport long-lived connection from TypeScript.
-
-**Non-goal**: do not modify `core-ffi`'s C ABI or any mxcore internal crate. The binding is a pure consumer.
-
----
-
-## 2. Decisions (brainstorming outcomes)
-
-| # | Question | Decision | Rationale |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| 1 | Binding strategy | **napi-rs** native module | Type-safe, async-native, ThreadsafeFunction handles the rng/info reverse-callback cleanly; ffi-napi was rejected (semi-abandoned, manual struct shims, callback-thread pain) |
-| 2 | Functional scope | **All 4 blocks** (IKey, decodePushFrame, AppContext, PushTransport) | Rust ABI surface is already complete; binding once, end-to-end |
-| 3 | Platforms | **Win x64 + macOS arm64** | Win = primary Electron target; macOS arm64 = dev box. No CI matrix yet |
-| 4 | JS API style | **Idiomatic JS** (classes, EventEmitter, Promise, TS discriminated unions) | Hides opaque handles + manual free; matches Node ergonomics |
-| 5 | Repo layout & distribution | **In-repo, local build** (`@napi-rs/cli` standard layout) | Mirrors `bindings/swift/`; no npm registry yet; upgrade to GH Actions matrix is non-breaking |
-
----
-
-## 3. Architecture
-
-```
-+-------------------+
-|  Electron app     |  TS:  import { PushTransport, IKey, AppContext } from '@mxcore/native'
-+-------------------+
-         | JS class methods
-         v
-+-------------------+
-|  index.js (napi)  |  loads mxcore.win32-x64.node OR mxcore.darwin-arm64.node by process.platform/arch
-+-------------------+
-         |
-         v
-+----------------------------+
-|  bindings/electron (Rust)  |  napi-rs crate
-|  - IKey class              |  → core_crypto::ikey::IKey
-|  - decodePushFrame fn      |  → core_ffi::ingest::decode_push_frame
-|  - AppContext class        |  → core_context::AppContext
-|  - PushTransport class     |  → core_transport::PushTransport
-|  - ThreadsafeFunction × 2  |  rng / info callbacks (tokio worker → V8)
-|  - Event bridge            |  EventEmitter-style fan-out (9 event kinds)
-+----------------------------+
-         | rlib link (Rust API, NOT C ABI)
-         v
-+----------------------------+
-|  core-ffi + mxcore crates  |  unchanged
-+----------------------------+
-```
-
-**Key invariants**:
-- Binding does NOT call `mx_*` C functions; it `use`s the Rust API directly. C ABI stays Swift-binding-only.
-- No mxcore internal crate is modified.
-- napi-rs and mxcore share one tokio runtime (`napi/features = ["tokio_rt"]`).
