-## 6. Internal implementation notes
-
-### 6.1 Files
-
-| File | Responsibility |
-|---|---|
-| `error.rs` | `to_napi(code: i32) -> napi::Error` — symbol+code stringification |
-| `ikey.rs` | Wraps `core_crypto::ikey::IKey` as `#[napi]` class. Buffer share-no-copy via napi-rs `Buffer` |
-| `frame.rs` | Calls `core_ffi::ingest::decode_push_frame`; returns `#[napi(object)]` plain JS objects |
-| `app_context.rs` | Wraps `core_context::AppContext`. Holds `Arc<AppContext>` to allow future supervisor `with_server_clock` injection without ABI break |
-| `threadsafe.rs` | `RngCallback` / `InfoCallback` ThreadsafeFunction with sync-return-value bridge |
-| `transport.rs` | `PushTransport` class + event-loop tokio task + EventEmitter-style `on(name, cb)` |
-
-### 6.2 ThreadsafeFunction (rng / info) — sync return value
-
-mxcore supervisor calls these callbacks **synchronously** from a tokio worker; we cannot `block_on` V8. Pattern:
-
-```rust
-fn rng_callback_bridge(tsfn: &RngCallback, n: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
-    let (tx, rx) = std::sync::mpsc::sync_channel::<Vec<u8>>(0);
-    tsfn.call_with_return_value(
-        n,
-        ThreadsafeFunctionCallMode::Blocking,
-        move |js_buf: Buffer| { tx.send(js_buf.to_vec()).ok(); Ok(()) },
-    );
-    rx.recv_timeout(Duration::from_secs(5)).unwrap_or_default()
-}
-```
-
-- Timeout = mxcore `PUSH_REG_TIMEOUT` (5s). Empty Vec on timeout → mxcore takes `GarbledResponse` path.
-- **JS callbacks must be sync**. No `async`, no `Promise`. Documented in §5.5. Rationale: rng is sync-by-nature; PushRegInfo is in-memory state in Electron. If future need arises, add a `_async` variant.
-- libuv/V8 thread ≠ tokio worker, so `std::sync::mpsc` is safe (no deadlock).
-
-### 6.3 PushTransport event loop
-
-- On `PushTransport::create`, spawn one tokio task on the napi-shared runtime that loops `transport.next_event().await`.
-- Each event is matched on kind, mapped to a `#[napi(object)]` payload, and dispatched to all registered ThreadsafeFunctions for that event name.
-- `on(name, cb)` registers a TSFN per (event-name, callback) pair, stored in `Arc<Mutex<HashMap<String, Vec<TSFN>>>>`.
-- `Drop` impl signals shutdown via `tokio::sync::oneshot`; the event-loop task awaits `transport.shutdown()` for graceful cleanup before exit.
-- Bounded internal channel (mpsc 64) matching mxcore stage 3 A3 decision.
-
-### 6.4 EventEmitter style without extending Node EventEmitter
-
-`#[napi]` exposes `fn on(&self, event: String, cb: napi::JsFunction) -> napi::Result<()>` directly. JS-side usage is identical to `EventEmitter.on`, but no JS wrapper class is needed. No `off` / `once` / `removeAllListeners` in v1 (YAGNI) — to be added if Electron app needs them.
-
-### 6.5 Drop / lifecycle
-
-- `IKey`, `AppContext`, `PushTransport` are `#[napi]` classes. napi-rs auto-generates `Drop` glue → underlying Rust drops normally.
-- `PushTransport::Drop` triggers async shutdown via oneshot signal; event-loop task does the await. Worst case: 500ms graceful + abort fallback (matches mxcore stage 5 P0-4 semantic).
