-## 7. Build, test, distribution
-
-### 7.1 Local build
-
-```sh
-cd bindings/electron
-npm install
-npm run build              # release (host triple)
-npm run build:debug
-```
-
-`napi build --platform`:
-1. `cargo build --release --target <host-triple>`
-2. Renames `target/<triple>/release/mxcore_electron.{dll,dylib}` → `mxcore.<platform>-<arch>.node`
-3. Places it next to `index.js` for runtime loading.
-
-**No cross-compile**. Producing the macOS .node requires a macOS host; the Win64 .node requires a Windows host.
-
-### 7.2 Electron consumption
-
-```json
-"dependencies": { "@mxcore/native": "file:../mxcore-proposal/bindings/electron" }
-```
-
-or `npm link`. `require('@mxcore/native')` auto-loads platform-specific `.node`.
-
-### 7.3 Test plan
-
-Tests live in `bindings/electron/__tests__/`. Tool: `vitest` (runs in plain Node — no Electron renderer).
-
-| File | Verifies |
-|---|---|
-| `ikey.test.ts` | Encrypt/decrypt round-trip with same fixtures as `core-crypto` unit tests |
-| `frame.test.ts` | `decodePushFrame` against `core-protocol` fixture frames; expect byte-equal payloadJson |
-| `app_context.test.ts` | login/logout, `clockSync` forward-only enforcement, `MX_ERR_*` thrown |
-| `transport-loopback.test.ts` | Local Node TCP server mimicking push server (mirrors mxcore `inmemory_duplex` happy-path) |
-| `transport-callbacks.test.ts` | rng/info called from native, return values land in PushReg, 5s timeout path |
-| `transport-events.test.ts` | All 9 event kinds reach JS; events stop after `shutdown()` |
-
-mxcore's own 312 tests are NOT duplicated — binding tests verify only the JS↔Rust bridge.
-
-### 7.4 Coexistence with `bindings/swift/`
-
-- `bindings/swift/` and `bindings/electron/` live side-by-side, fully independent.
-- `core-ffi` produces both `staticlib` (for Swift xcframework) and `lib`/rlib (for napi-rs). Cargo emits both in one build; no conflict.
-- `mxcore.h` is **not** read by the binding. Future C ABI changes don't affect the Electron binding (binding consumes Rust API directly; compile errors surface breakage immediately).
-
-### 7.5 Out of scope (YAGNI)
-
-- ❌ GitHub Actions CI matrix
-- ❌ npm publish / private registry
-- ❌ Linux / Win arm64 / Intel Mac builds
-- ❌ Raw C ABI escape-hatch in JS
-- ❌ `core-storage` / `core-workspace` exposure (Phase 2)
-- ❌ SQLCipher feature flag pass-through
-- ❌ Async JS callbacks for rng / info (Promise return)
-- ❌ `EventEmitter.off` / `once` / `removeAllListeners`
