-## 8. Risks & mitigations
-
-| Risk | Mitigation |
-|---|---|
-| napi-rs major version drift breaking ABI | Pin `napi = "2"` (current stable line); upgrade only with full test re-run |
-| ThreadsafeFunction sync-return deadlock if JS callback throws | TSFN call wraps in `Result`; on JS exception, sender drops → `recv_timeout` returns empty → mxcore `GarbledResponse` path |
-| Two tokio runtimes (napi default + mxcore) | `tokio_rt` feature shares one runtime; verified by `napi-rs` docs |
-| `Buffer` lifetime mismatch (V8 GC vs Rust borrow) | napi-rs `Buffer` ref-counts the underlying ArrayBuffer; safe across `await` boundaries |
-| Event flood overwhelming V8 (high reconnect churn) | Bounded mpsc(64) + ThreadsafeFunction blocking call back-pressures the supervisor |
-| `Drop` running on V8 main thread blocking UI | Shutdown is fire-and-forget; oneshot signal + tokio task does await; main thread doesn't block |
-| Win64 build chain (MSVC vs MinGW) | Standardize on MSVC (`x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`); document in README |
-
----
-
-## 9. Acceptance criteria
-
-1. `cd bindings/electron && npm install && npm run build` produces `mxcore.<platform>-<arch>.node` on Win x64 host AND macOS arm64 host.
-2. `npm test` passes all 6 test files on both hosts.
-3. A minimal Electron renderer or main-process script can:
-   - Construct `IKey`, encrypt + decrypt a buffer
-   - Call `decodePushFrame` on a known-good fixture
-   - Construct `AppContext`, log in, call `clockSync`, observe `serverNowMs()` advancing
-   - Construct `PushTransport`, connect to a local loopback server, register, send a frame, receive an event, shutdown
-4. No changes to `core-ffi` C ABI, `mxcore.h`, or `bindings/swift/`.
-5. mxcore workspace `cargo test` still 312 passed / 0 failed / 1 ignored (binding lives outside `default-members`).
