-## 11. Implementation deviations from §5 / §6 (post-Task-11 mxcore tracking)
-
-The §5 / §6 API shapes were specified against a snapshot of mxcore. As mxcore landed Task-11 work (signal-channel unification, D6 PushReg reversal, AppContext expansion), the binding tracked each upstream change. Recording here so future readers don't re-derive these from git history.
-
-### 11.1 Wire-format constants (Task 4 implementation)
-
-| Spec said | Reality |
-|---|---|
-| MAGIC = `0x564E` | `0x270F` (per `core_protocol::frame::MAGIC`) |
-| NEED_ACK = `0x0001` | `1 << 1 = 0x0002` (per `core_protocol::frame::Flags::NEED_ACK`) |
-
-Frame fixture in `__tests__/frame.test.ts` was corrected accordingly. Rust `inflate` accepts Node `deflateRawSync` output despite different DEFLATE-block strategies (verified byte-equal round-trip).
-
-### 11.2 IKey constructor (Task 3)
-
-| Spec said | Reality |
-|---|---|
-| `new IKey(secretKey: Buffer)` | `new IKey(secretKey: Buffer, uid: string)` — uid is required HKDF salt |
-| `encryptCBC` / `decryptCBC` / `encryptIM` / `decryptIM` | `encryptPush` / `decryptPush` / `encryptUserData` / `decryptUserData` (matches `core_crypto::IKey` pub method names) |
-
-### 11.3 AppContext shape (Task 5 + commit `fcd1d16`)
-
-§5.4's flat 13-field `AppContextInit` mapped 1:1 onto `AppInfo::new` + `DeviceInfo::new` + `LocaleSettings::new`. After mxcore expanded the builder with `environment_label` / `endpoint_config` / `pin_config` (required) and `is_appex` / `initial_network_kind` / `initial_device_key` (optional), the binding added 4 new fields:
-
-```ts
-interface AppContextInit {
-  // ... existing 12 fields
-  environmentLabel: string;          // required, non-empty
-  isAppex?: boolean;                 // default false
-  initialNetworkKind?: string;       // "none" | "wifi" | "wired" | "2g" | ... | "vpn" | "other"
-  initialDeviceKey?: string;
-}
-```
-
-Also: `login()` argument order is `(userId, rid, spaceId)` matching `UserSession::new(uid, rid, space_id)` — the spec implied `(userId, workspaceId)` (2 args).
-
-### 11.4 PushTransport `create()` signature (commit `fcd1d16`, BREAKING)
-
-D6 reversal in mxcore (CLAUDE.md `core-context-app-context-server-clock` spec §12.14) removed the PushReg `info` callback — modules must source identity from `Arc<AppContext>` directly. The binding followed:
-
-```ts
-// Spec §5.5 (original)
-PushTransport.create({
-  addresses, initialNetworkAvailable, preferAddress?,
-  onNeedRegisterInfo: () => PushRegInfo,    // REMOVED
-  onNeedRandom: (n) => Buffer,
-  backoff?,
-}): Promise<PushTransport>;
-
-// Reality (positional args, sync return)
-PushTransport.create(
-  addresses: PushAddress[],
-  ikey: IKey,
-  appContext: AppContext,                   // NEW (replaces onNeedRegisterInfo)
-  deviceTypeByte: number,
-  initialNetworkAvailable: boolean,
-  onNeedRandom: (n: number) => Buffer,
-  backoff?: BackoffOpts,
-): PushTransport;
-```
-
-Identity, locale, network kind, device key, user session — all snapshotted from `AppContext` per dial cycle. Bindings populate `AppContext` BEFORE calling `create`.
-
-### 11.5 PushTransport methods became sync (commit `fcd1d16`)
-
-mxcore replaced the bounded `mpsc::Sender<Outbound>` with an unbounded `mpsc::UnboundedSender<SupervisorSignal>`. The binding's outbound methods no longer have anything to `.await`:
-
-```ts
-// Spec §5.5 (original)
-sendFrame(body: Buffer): Promise<void>;
-reconnect(): Promise<void>;
-forceClose(): Promise<void>;
-setNetworkAvailable(available: boolean): Promise<void>;
-
-// Reality (sync, no Promise)
-sendFrame(body: Buffer): void;
-reconnect(): void;
-forceClose(): void;
-setNetworkAvailable(available: boolean): void;
-setAppForeground(isFg: boolean): void;     // NEW — H1 proactive heartbeat trigger
-shutdown(): Promise<void>;                  // STILL async (awaits supervisor + event-loop joins, 500ms timeout)
-```
-
-JS callers can drop `await` on the sync four. Existing `await transport.sendFrame(...)` still works (await on non-Promise resolves to the value).
-
-### 11.6 Event taxonomy expansion (commits `8958a37` + `fcd1d16`)
-
-`TransportEvent` grew from §5.5's listed 9 kinds to the current 22 surfaced via `event_to_payload`. New kinds (all already wired):
-
-- `Status { previous, current }` — was tuple `Status(state)`; now exposes both fields
-- `DisconnectReason` +3 variants: `AckTimeout` / `DispatchFailed` / `DecodeFailed`
-- Diagnostics: `frameReceived`, `pushRegEncoded`, `pushRegWire`, `pushRegZipMeta`, `wireTx`, `wireRx`, `heartbeatSent`, `networkAvailabilityChanged`, `dialStarted`, `dialFailed`, `ackReceived`, `proactiveHeartbeat`, `sendResult`, `sendPoorNetwork`, `ackTimeoutReconnect` (subset; full list lives in `transport_events.rs::decompose`)
-
-JS payload format unchanged: `{ name: string; payloadJson: string; body?: Buffer }`. Future `#[non_exhaustive]` variants surface as `name === "unknown"` rather than panic.
-
-### 11.7 No more `ChannelAvailability` bridge (commit `fcd1d16`)
-
-Spec §6 implied an `Arc<ChannelAvailability>` would live in `PushTransport` so JS-side `setNetworkAvailable` could publish via `tokio::watch`. mxcore unified this into `SupervisorSignal::SetNetworkAvailable(bool)` — the binding now sends straight through `signal_tx`, and `ChannelAvailability` / `AvailabilityBridge` are deleted.
-
-### 11.8 PushOs enum is `Ios | Mac` only
-
-`core_protocol::pushreg::PushOs` has only two variants. Windows / Android Electron callers must use `'mac'` for the wire `os` field. Documented in `threadsafe.rs` head comment (now mostly historical since the info callback is gone — `os` is sourced from `AppContext::app_info().client_type()`).
-
-### 11.9 napi-rs `Option<String>` + `null`
-
-Calling JS-side with `tenantId: null` triggers a `StringExpected` fatal in the TSFN return-value converter. Use `undefined` (or omit the field). This bit us in Task 8 and is documented in the loopback fixture comment.
